    {
      "id": "MAT-SNS-M001",
      "subject": "Mathematics",
      "chapter": "Sequence & Series",
      "topic": "Arithmetico-Geometric Infinite Series Sums",
      "category": "Sequence & Series :: Advanced Mathematical Structure (Type 1)",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "type": "mcq",
      "question": "Find the sum of the infinite arithmetico-geometric series (AGP) in [Sequence & Series]:\n$$S = 1 + \\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{3}{3^2} + \\frac{4}{3^3} + \\dots$$",
      "options": [
        "$\\frac{9}{4}$",
        "$\\frac{3}{2}$",
        "$\\frac{9}{2}$",
        "$2$"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "$S = 1 + \\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{3}{9} + \\dots$ and $\\frac{1}{3}S = \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{2}{9} + \\dots$. Subtracting gives $\\frac{2}{3}S = 1 + \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{9} + \\dots = \\frac{1}{1 - 1/3} = \\frac{3}{2} \\implies S = \\frac{3}{2} \\times \\frac{3}{2} = \\frac{9}{4}$.",
      "explanation": "Solve using rigorous mathematical proofs and transformations in Sequence & Series.",
      "possibleErrorType": "Formula mistake",
      "isReactionBased": false,
      "image": null,
      "source": "question_bank",
      "tags": [
        "JEE Main",
        "JEE Advanced",
